  <Properties>
    <pageHeading>
      <Value><![CDATA[About this prototype]]></Value>
    </pageHeading>
    <lede>
      <Value><![CDATA[This site shows how a GOV.UK-styled service can be built and managed in Umbraco.]]></Value>
    </lede>
    <bodyText>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "markup": "<h2>What it includes</h2><ul><li>Umbraco 17 LTS on .NET 10, using SQLite</li><li>GOV.UK Frontend components rendered by tag helpers and Umbraco blocks</li><li>Example pages recreated from the govuk-frontend-aspnetcore-extensions example application</li><li>The Umbraco Developer MCP server, so an AI assistant can manage content types and content</li></ul><h2>How pages are built</h2><p>Component example pages use the GOV.UK block list and block grid editors. Content pages like this one use ordinary properties rendered by a Razor template using <a href=\"https://github.com/x-govuk/govuk-frontend-aspnetcore\">GOV.UK Frontend tag helpers</a>.</p>",
  "blocks": null
}]]></Value>
    </bodyText>
    <insetText>
      <Value><![CDATA[This is a local prototype. It is not a real government service.]]></Value>
    </insetText>
  </Properties>
</Content>
